<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>Follow the Rupee</name><description>Follow the Rupee, Claude Impact Lab Mumbai. Synthetic data; all contractors are fictional.</description><Style id="grade-A"><LineStyle><color>ffffffff</color><width>1.5</width></LineStyle><PolyStyle><color>a6449e2f</color></PolyStyle></Style><Style id="grade-B"><LineStyle><color>ffffffff</color><width>1.5</width></LineStyle><PolyStyle><color>a616b874</color></PolyStyle></Style><Style id="grade-C"><LineStyle><color>ffffffff</color><width>1.5</width></LineStyle><PolyStyle><color>a6009ff5</color></PolyStyle></Style><Style id="grade-D"><LineStyle><color>ffffffff</color><width>1.5</width></LineStyle><PolyStyle><color>a60767f7</color></PolyStyle></Style><Style id="grade-E"><LineStyle><color>ffffffff</color><width>1.5</width></LineStyle><PolyStyle><color>a63131e0</color></PolyStyle></Style><Style id="road-flagged"><LineStyle><color>ff3131e0</color><width>5</width></LineStyle></Style><Style id="road-dlp"><LineStyle><color>ff0767f7</color><width>5</width></LineStyle></Style><Style id="road-plain"><LineStyle><color>ff9e958e</color><width>3</width></LineStyle></Style><Style id="fix"><IconStyle><color>ff0f48d9</color><scale>1.1</scale><Icon><href>https://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/shapes/caution.png</href></Icon></IconStyle></Style><Folder><name>Wards, coloured by grade</name><Placemark><name>Ward A · grade C</name><styleUrl>#grade-C</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Grade C</b> (47 of 100; 50 is as expected for these jobs)<br/>Spent ₹16,55,330 of ₹16,00,000 (103%) on 29 jobs<br/>On fixes that failed within 30 days: ₹5,82,099<br/>In question: ₹4,06,680 (1 over-billed, 1 duplicates, 9 paid under DLP)<br/>Open problems past their SLA: 4<br/><br/>Ward A (Colaba, Fort, Churchgate) scores 47, grade C; a score of 50 means &quot;as expected for these jobs, given method, rain and ward.&quot; Across 29 jobs, ₹16,55,330 was spent against a ₹16,00,000 budget (103%), leaving it ₹55,330 over. Repairs held poorly: ₹5,82,099 went on fixes that failed within 30 days, and durability scored 30. Records put ₹4,06,680 in question: one bill above 1.5 times the rate card, one duplicate bill, and 9 payments (₹3,63,827) on roads still within the contractor's guarantee period. Four issues are open and overdue. Next fixes: first, replace the broken manhole cover on Veer Nariman Road (₹47,629), a severity 5 hazard near a school with a 24-hour deadline. Second, patch the Colaba Causeway pothole (₹16,437), which has 5 complaints, 21 &quot;me too&quot; votes and one accident. Third, patch the Veer Nariman Road pothole (₹16,437), where heavy traffic and 14 bus routes meet a prior accident.]]></description><ExtendedData><Data name="ward_code"><value>A</value></Data><Data name="ward_name"><value>Colaba, Fort, Churchgate</value></Data><Data name="zone"><value>Zone 1</value></Data><Data name="grade"><value>C</value></Data><Data name="score"><value>47</value></Data><Data name="budget_inr"><value>1600000</value></Data><Data name="spend_inr"><value>1655330</value></Data><Data name="money_in_question_inr"><value>406680</value></Data><Data name="open_overdue_issues"><value>4</value></Data></ExtendedData><Polygon><outerBoundaryIs><LinearRing><coordinates>72.805,18.895 72.84,18.895 72.85335,18.93729 72.84139,18.93866 72.80305,18.93044 72.799,18.92799 72.805,18.895</coordinates></LinearRing></outerBoundaryIs></Polygon></Placemark><Placemark><name>Ward B · grade C</name><styleUrl>#grade-C</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Grade C</b> (58 of 100; 50 is as expected for these jobs)<br/>Spent ₹35,07,952 of ₹43,00,000 (82%) on 44 jobs<br/>On fixes that failed within 30 days: ₹5,78,915<br/>In question: ₹5,74,135 (5 over-billed, 0 duplicates, 3 paid under DLP)<br/>Open problems past their SLA: 7<br/><br/>Ward B (Dongri, Masjid Bunder) scores 58, grade C, where 50 means as expected for these jobs given method, rain and ward. Of the ₹43,00,000 budget, ₹35,07,952 (82%) has been spent on 44 jobs, leaving ₹7,92,048. Repairs held only partly: durability scored 55, and ₹5,78,915 went on fixes that failed within 30 days. Records put ₹5,74,135 in question. Five bills were above 1.5 times the rate card, and three payments, ₹1,73,383, were made on roads still within the contractor's guarantee period. No duplicate bills were found. Seven issues are open and overdue. Next fixes: first, the Mohammed Ali Road manhole (₹47,629), a severity 5 issue on the ambulance road to Sir JJ Hospital. Second, desilting P D'Mello Road (₹73,252), which is near a school and a flood-prone spot. Third, patching the Nishanpada Road pothole (₹16,437), which has 66 &quot;me too&quot; reports and the same flood risk.]]></description><ExtendedData><Data name="ward_code"><value>B</value></Data><Data name="ward_name"><value>Dongri, Masjid Bunder</value></Data><Data name="zone"><value>Zone 1</value></Data><Data name="grade"><value>C</value></Data><Data name="score"><value>58</value></Data><Data name="budget_inr"><value>4300000</value></Data><Data name="spend_inr"><value>3507952</value></Data><Data name="money_in_question_inr"><value>574135</value></Data><Data name="open_overdue_issues"><value>7</value></Data></ExtendedData><Polygon><outerBoundaryIs><LinearRing><coordinates>72.85335,18.93729 72.86457,18.97279 72.82383,18.96374 72.84139,18.93866 72.85335,18.93729</coordinates></LinearRing></outerBoundaryIs></Polygon></Placemark><Placemark><name>Ward C · grade D</name><styleUrl>#grade-D</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Grade D</b> (33 of 100; 50 is as expected for these jobs)<br/>Spent ₹7,96,803 of ₹9,00,000 (88%) on 20 jobs<br/>On fixes that failed within 30 days: ₹2,47,660<br/>In question: ₹1,90,409 (2 over-billed, 0 duplicates, 5 paid under DLP)<br/>Open problems past their SLA: 8<br/><br/>Ward C (Kalbadevi, Bhuleshwar, Marine Lines) gets grade D, with an overall score of 33, where 50 means as expected for these jobs given method, rain and ward. Of the ₹9,00,000 budget, ₹7,96,803 (88%) has gone on 20 jobs, leaving ₹1,03,197. The repairs have not held well: durability scored 26, and ₹2,47,660 was spent on fixes that failed within 30 days. Eight issues are open and overdue. ₹1,90,409 is in question because two bills were above 1.5 times the rate card, and five payments totalling ₹1,83,276 were made on roads still within the contractor's guarantee period (DLP). No duplicate bills were found. Next, fix three open manholes, each a severity 5 issue with a 24-hour limit. Nepean Sea Road and Princess Street (₹47,629 each) both had an accident last year and are near schools. Kalbadevi Road is near a school and has one complaint backed by 31 &quot;me too&quot; reports. The original contractor should be called back to fix it under the guarantee at no cost.]]></description><ExtendedData><Data name="ward_code"><value>C</value></Data><Data name="ward_name"><value>Kalbadevi, Bhuleshwar, Marine Lines</value></Data><Data name="zone"><value>Zone 1</value></Data><Data name="grade"><value>D</value></Data><Data name="score"><value>33</value></Data><Data name="budget_inr"><value>900000</value></Data><Data name="spend_inr"><value>796803</value></Data><Data name="money_in_question_inr"><value>190409</value></Data><Data name="open_overdue_issues"><value>8</value></Data></ExtendedData><Polygon><outerBoundaryIs><LinearRing><coordinates>72.80305,18.93044 72.84139,18.93866 72.82383,18.96374 72.82279,18.96399 72.80305,18.93044</coordinates></LinearRing></outerBoundaryIs></Polygon></Placemark><Placemark><name>Ward D · grade D</name><styleUrl>#grade-D</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Grade D</b> (44 of 100; 50 is as expected for these jobs)<br/>Spent ₹12,72,300 of ₹16,00,000 (80%) on 40 jobs<br/>On fixes that failed within 30 days: ₹2,35,027<br/>In question: ₹5,40,368 (1 over-billed, 1 duplicates, 11 paid under DLP)<br/>Open problems past their SLA: 5<br/><br/>Ward D (Grant Road, Malabar Hill, Tardeo) scores 44, grade D, where 50 means as expected for these jobs, given method, rain and ward. Of the ₹16,00,000 budget, ₹12,72,300 (80%) is spent on 40 jobs, leaving ₹3,27,700. Repairs held fairly well (durability 61), but billing scored 11. ₹5,40,368 is in question: 11 payments (₹5,25,710) were made on roads still under the contractor's guarantee period, one bill was above 1.5 times the rate card, and one was a duplicate. Also, ₹2,35,027 went on fixes that failed within 30 days, and 5 issues are open and overdue. Next fixes: Pandita Ramabai Road waterlogging, at no cost, by calling the original contractor under the guarantee, as it is a severity 4 issue near a school; Peddar Road pothole, ₹16,437, for heavy traffic and one accident; Tardeo Road pothole, ₹16,437, with 39 &quot;me too&quot; reports.]]></description><ExtendedData><Data name="ward_code"><value>D</value></Data><Data name="ward_name"><value>Grant Road, Malabar Hill, Tardeo</value></Data><Data name="zone"><value>Zone 1</value></Data><Data name="grade"><value>D</value></Data><Data name="score"><value>44</value></Data><Data name="budget_inr"><value>1600000</value></Data><Data name="spend_inr"><value>1272300</value></Data><Data name="money_in_question_inr"><value>540368</value></Data><Data name="open_overdue_issues"><value>5</value></Data></ExtendedData><Polygon><outerBoundaryIs><LinearRing><coordinates>72.80039,18.98595 72.795,18.95 72.799,18.92799 72.80305,18.93044 72.82279,18.96399 72.81,18.9836 72.80039,18.98595</coordinates></LinearRing></outerBoundaryIs></Polygon></Placemark><Placemark><name>Ward E · grade D</name><styleUrl>#grade-D</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Grade D</b> (40 of 100; 50 is as expected for these jobs)<br/>Spent ₹63,22,991 of ₹53,00,000 (119%) on 118 jobs<br/>On fixes that failed within 30 days: ₹20,11,624<br/>In question: ₹26,93,520 (9 over-billed, 2 duplicates, 41 paid under DLP)<br/>Open problems past their SLA: 19<br/><br/>Ward E (Byculla, Agripada, Mumbai Central) scores 40, grade D, where 50 means as expected for these jobs, given method, rain and ward. Against a budget of ₹53,00,000, ₹63,22,991 has been spent on 118 jobs (119%), which is ₹10,22,991 over. Repairs often did not hold: ₹20,11,624 went on fixes that failed within 30 days. In question is ₹26,93,520. The records show 9 bills above 1.5 times the rate card, 2 duplicate bills, and 41 payments (₹24,96,332) made on roads still within the contractor's guarantee period. 19 issues remain open and overdue. The next three fixes are all on Bellasis Road, the ambulance route to BYL Nair Hospital, near Byculla Station West, which flooded above 100 mm on 14 days last season. First, the cave-in (₹1,93,560); second, the broken manhole (₹47,629). Both are severity 5 issues with a 24-hour deadline. Third, the choked drain (₹73,252), which has 87 &quot;me too&quot; reports.]]></description><ExtendedData><Data name="ward_code"><value>E</value></Data><Data name="ward_name"><value>Byculla, Agripada, Mumbai Central</value></Data><Data name="zone"><value>Zone 1</value></Data><Data name="grade"><value>D</value></Data><Data name="score"><value>40</value></Data><Data name="budget_inr"><value>5300000</value></Data><Data name="spend_inr"><value>6322991</value></Data><Data name="money_in_question_inr"><value>2693520</value></Data><Data name="open_overdue_issues"><value>19</value></Data></ExtendedData><Polygon><outerBoundaryIs><LinearRing><coordinates>72.86457,18.97279 72.8656,18.97606 72.82837,18.99095 72.81,18.9836 72.82279,18.96399 72.82383,18.96374 72.86457,18.97279</coordinates></LinearRing></outerBoundaryIs></Polygon></Placemark><Placemark><name>Ward F/S · grade C</name><styleUrl>#grade-C</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Grade C</b> (55 of 100; 50 is as expected for these jobs)<br/>Spent ₹80,26,151 of ₹98,00,000 (82%) on 135 jobs<br/>On fixes that failed within 30 days: ₹13,35,554<br/>In question: ₹10,28,873 (7 over-billed, 2 duplicates, 14 paid under DLP)<br/>Open problems past their SLA: 26<br/><br/>F/S ward (Parel, Lalbaug, Sewri) scores 55, grade C; a score of 50 means as expected for these jobs, given method, rain and ward. Of the ₹98,00,000 budget, ₹80,26,151 (82%) is spent across 135 jobs, leaving ₹17,73,849. Repairs mostly held (durability 67), but ₹13,35,554 went on fixes that failed within 30 days, and speed is weak at 36, with 26 overdue open issues. In question is ₹10,28,873: 7 bills above 1.5 times the rate card, 2 duplicate bills, and 14 payments (₹6,76,407) on roads still under the contractor's guarantee period. The next three fixes are all on Dr Babasaheb Ambedkar Road, 354 m from Hindmata Junction, which floods above 60 mm a day (17 such days last season). First, a dewatering pump (₹64,251) for waterlogging. Second, a manhole cover and grating (₹47,629), a 24-hour severity 5 hazard. Third, desilting the choked drain (₹73,252), since this is the ambulance road to KEM Hospital.]]></description><ExtendedData><Data name="ward_code"><value>F/S</value></Data><Data name="ward_name"><value>Parel, Lalbaug, Sewri</value></Data><Data name="zone"><value>Zone 2</value></Data><Data name="grade"><value>C</value></Data><Data name="score"><value>55</value></Data><Data name="budget_inr"><value>9800000</value></Data><Data name="spend_inr"><value>8026151</value></Data><Data name="money_in_question_inr"><value>1028873</value></Data><Data name="open_overdue_issues"><value>26</value></Data></ExtendedData><Polygon><outerBoundaryIs><LinearRing><coordinates>72.8656,18.97606 72.87,18.99 72.88427,18.99504 72.84267,19.02 72.83502,19.02019 72.82837,18.99095 72.8656,18.97606</coordinates></LinearRing></outerBoundaryIs></Polygon></Placemark><Placemark><name>Ward F/N · grade D</name><styleUrl>#grade-D</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Grade D</b> (43 of 100; 50 is as expected for these jobs)<br/>Spent ₹94,12,574 of ₹1,05,00,000 (90%) on 150 jobs<br/>On fixes that failed within 30 days: ₹21,34,363<br/>In question: ₹28,27,782 (6 over-billed, 3 duplicates, 37 paid under DLP)<br/>Open problems past their SLA: 32<br/><br/>F/N ward (Matunga, Sion, Wadala) scores 43 out of 100, grade D; 50 would mean as expected for these jobs, given method, rain and ward. Of the ₹1,05,00,000 budget, ₹94,12,574 (90%) is spent across 150 jobs, leaving ₹10,87,426. Repairs held up poorly: ₹21,34,363 went on fixes that failed within 30 days. Another ₹28,27,782 is in question: 6 bills above 1.5 times the rate card, 3 duplicate bills, and 37 payments (₹22,21,383) on roads still under the contractor's guarantee period. 32 issues are open and overdue. Next fixes: first, the open manhole on Eastern Express Highway (₹47,629), a severity 5 hazard near a flood-prone spot, with 3 accidents, 1 fatal. Second, waterlogging on Sion Trombay Road (₹64,251), near a school. Third, the pothole on the same highway (₹16,437), near LTMG Sion Hospital.]]></description><ExtendedData><Data name="ward_code"><value>F/N</value></Data><Data name="ward_name"><value>Matunga, Sion, Wadala</value></Data><Data name="zone"><value>Zone 2</value></Data><Data name="grade"><value>D</value></Data><Data name="score"><value>43</value></Data><Data name="budget_inr"><value>10500000</value></Data><Data name="spend_inr"><value>9412574</value></Data><Data name="money_in_question_inr"><value>2827782</value></Data><Data name="open_overdue_issues"><value>32</value></Data></ExtendedData><Polygon><outerBoundaryIs><LinearRing><coordinates>72.88427,18.99504 72.90508,19.00238 72.87598,19.04893 72.87449,19.04982 72.85976,19.04904 72.84267,19.02 72.88427,18.99504</coordinates></LinearRing></outerBoundaryIs></Polygon></Placemark><Placemark><name>Ward G/S · grade D</name><styleUrl>#grade-D</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Grade D</b> (39 of 100; 50 is as expected for these jobs)<br/>Spent ₹28,21,986 of ₹32,00,000 (88%) on 64 jobs<br/>On fixes that failed within 30 days: ₹10,57,467<br/>In question: ₹10,59,034 (0 over-billed, 0 duplicates, 21 paid under DLP)<br/>Open problems past their SLA: 14<br/><br/>G/S ward scores 39 (grade D); a score of 50 would mean as expected for these jobs, given method, rain and ward. Of the ₹32,00,000 budget, ₹28,21,986 (88%) is spent across 64 jobs, with Sahyadri Infra Works the largest by spend. Repairs held poorly: ₹10,57,467 went on fixes that failed within 30 days. In question is ₹10,59,034 paid on 21 roads still under the contractor's guarantee period (DLP), when repairs should be free. No bills were above 1.5 times the rate card and none were duplicates, but 14 issues are open and overdue. Next, on Senapati Bapat Marg: first, call the original contractor under the guarantee and deploy a pump for waterlogging, at ₹0, since it is a severity 4 issue near flood-prone Worli Naka, with 4 complaints. Second, a ₹64,251 pump nearby, where 3,805 vehicles and 23 bus routes pass at peak hour. Third, a free hot mix patch for a guaranteed pothole with 6 complaints.]]></description><ExtendedData><Data name="ward_code"><value>G/S</value></Data><Data name="ward_name"><value>Worli, Lower Parel, Prabhadevi</value></Data><Data name="zone"><value>Zone 2</value></Data><Data name="grade"><value>D</value></Data><Data name="score"><value>39</value></Data><Data name="budget_inr"><value>3200000</value></Data><Data name="spend_inr"><value>2821986</value></Data><Data name="money_in_question_inr"><value>1059034</value></Data><Data name="open_overdue_issues"><value>14</value></Data></ExtendedData><Polygon><outerBoundaryIs><LinearRing><coordinates>72.80817,19.0378 72.80039,18.98595 72.81,18.9836 72.82837,18.99095 72.83502,19.02019 72.80822,19.0378 72.80817,19.0378</coordinates></LinearRing></outerBoundaryIs></Polygon></Placemark><Placemark><name>Ward G/N · grade D</name><styleUrl>#grade-D</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Grade D</b> (44 of 100; 50 is as expected for these jobs)<br/>Spent ₹67,55,738 of ₹84,00,000 (80%) on 139 jobs<br/>On fixes that failed within 30 days: ₹17,29,109<br/>In question: ₹17,04,075 (3 over-billed, 7 duplicates, 23 paid under DLP)<br/>Open problems past their SLA: 25<br/><br/>G/N ward (Dadar West, Mahim, Dharavi) scores 44 out of 100, grade D, where 50 means as expected for these jobs given method, rain and ward. Of the ₹84,00,000 budget, ₹67,55,738 (80%) is spent across 139 jobs, leaving ₹16,44,262. Repairs did not hold well: ₹17,29,109 went on fixes that failed within 30 days. Records put ₹17,04,075 in question, including 3 bills above 1.5 times the rate card, 7 duplicate bills, and 23 payments (₹9,86,130) on roads still under the contractor's guarantee period (DLP). Also, 25 issues are open and overdue. The next three fixes are: waterlogging on Senapati Bapat Marg (₹64,251), a 48-hour issue with 2 accidents on the ambulance road to Mahim Fever Hospital; the pothole on the same road (₹16,437), with 13 complaints; and the broken manhole on 90 Feet Road Dharavi, a 24-hour issue near a school, which the original contractor should fix under DLP at ₹0.]]></description><ExtendedData><Data name="ward_code"><value>G/N</value></Data><Data name="ward_name"><value>Dadar West, Mahim, Dharavi</value></Data><Data name="zone"><value>Zone 2</value></Data><Data name="grade"><value>D</value></Data><Data name="score"><value>44</value></Data><Data name="budget_inr"><value>8400000</value></Data><Data name="spend_inr"><value>6755738</value></Data><Data name="money_in_question_inr"><value>1704075</value></Data><Data name="open_overdue_issues"><value>25</value></Data></ExtendedData><Polygon><outerBoundaryIs><LinearRing><coordinates>72.80822,19.0378 72.83502,19.02019 72.84267,19.02 72.85976,19.04904 72.84503,19.05693 72.80822,19.0378</coordinates></LinearRing></outerBoundaryIs></Polygon></Placemark><Placemark><name>Ward H/E · grade C</name><styleUrl>#grade-C</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Grade C</b> (52 of 100; 50 is as expected for these jobs)<br/>Spent ₹61,45,533 of ₹82,00,000 (75%) on 111 jobs<br/>On fixes that failed within 30 days: ₹16,12,052<br/>In question: ₹13,40,927 (6 over-billed, 5 duplicates, 17 paid under DLP)<br/>Open problems past their SLA: 16<br/><br/>H/E ward (Bandra East, Santacruz East, Khar East) scores 52, grade C, where 50 means as expected for these jobs, given method, rain and ward. Of the ₹82,00,000 budget, ₹61,45,533 (75%) is spent across 111 jobs, leaving ₹20,54,467. Durability is the weakest area at 47: ₹16,12,052 went on fixes that failed within 30 days. ₹13,40,927 is in question: 6 bills were above 1.5 times the rate card, 5 bills are duplicates, and 17 payments (₹8,96,301) were made on roads still under the contractor's guarantee period. 16 issues remain open and overdue. Next fixes: replace the broken manhole cover on Vakola Bridge Road (severity 5, 1,847 peak-hour vehicles); do the same on Kalanagar Road, near a municipal school; then deploy a dewatering pump on Vakola Bridge Road, which has 28 bus routes.]]></description><ExtendedData><Data name="ward_code"><value>H/E</value></Data><Data name="ward_name"><value>Bandra East, Santacruz East, Khar East</value></Data><Data name="zone"><value>Zone 3</value></Data><Data name="grade"><value>C</value></Data><Data name="score"><value>52</value></Data><Data name="budget_inr"><value>8200000</value></Data><Data name="spend_inr"><value>6145533</value></Data><Data name="money_in_question_inr"><value>1340927</value></Data><Data name="open_overdue_issues"><value>16</value></Data></ExtendedData><Polygon><outerBoundaryIs><LinearRing><coordinates>72.86847,19.09046 72.84149,19.09448 72.84102,19.09429 72.84503,19.05693 72.85976,19.04904 72.87449,19.04982 72.86847,19.09046</coordinates></LinearRing></outerBoundaryIs></Polygon></Placemark><Placemark><name>Ward H/W · grade D</name><styleUrl>#grade-D</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Grade D</b> (35 of 100; 50 is as expected for these jobs)<br/>Spent ₹42,45,242 of ₹43,00,000 (99%) on 62 jobs<br/>On fixes that failed within 30 days: ₹13,91,670<br/>In question: ₹22,83,487 (1 over-billed, 1 duplicates, 29 paid under DLP)<br/>Open problems past their SLA: 10<br/><br/>Ward H/W scored 35 (grade D); a score of 50 would mean as expected for these jobs, given method, rain and ward. Of the ₹43,00,000 budget, ₹42,45,242 (99%) is spent across 62 jobs, leaving ₹54,758. Repairs held only partly: ₹13,91,670 went on fixes that failed within 30 days. Records show ₹22,83,487 in question. This includes 29 payments totalling ₹22,37,982 made on roads still within the contractor's guarantee period, one bill above 1.5 times the rate card, and one duplicate bill. Ten issues remain open and overdue. The next three fixes are all on Linking Road, near KB Bhabha Hospital, where 2 road-condition accidents happened in 2024-25, one fatal. First, the open manhole (₹47,629), a severity 5 issue with a 24-hour deadline. Second, a pothole (₹16,437), with 26 &quot;me too&quot; reports. Third, broken paver blocks (₹59,705), with 38.]]></description><ExtendedData><Data name="ward_code"><value>H/W</value></Data><Data name="ward_name"><value>Bandra West, Khar West, Santacruz West</value></Data><Data name="zone"><value>Zone 3</value></Data><Data name="grade"><value>D</value></Data><Data name="score"><value>35</value></Data><Data name="budget_inr"><value>4300000</value></Data><Data name="spend_inr"><value>4245242</value></Data><Data name="money_in_question_inr"><value>2283487</value></Data><Data name="open_overdue_issues"><value>10</value></Data></ExtendedData><Polygon><outerBoundaryIs><LinearRing><coordinates>72.80527,19.09727 72.81,19.05 72.80817,19.0378 72.80822,19.0378 72.84503,19.05693 72.84102,19.09429 72.80527,19.09727</coordinates></LinearRing></outerBoundaryIs></Polygon></Placemark><Placemark><name>Ward K/E · grade B</name><styleUrl>#grade-B</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Grade B</b> (64 of 100; 50 is as expected for these jobs)<br/>Spent ₹82,64,048 of ₹91,00,000 (91%) on 165 jobs<br/>On fixes that failed within 30 days: ₹17,41,105<br/>In question: ₹4,02,110 (3 over-billed, 2 duplicates, 7 paid under DLP)<br/>Open problems past their SLA: 29<br/><br/>K/E ward earns a B (64; a score of 50 means as expected for these jobs, given method, rain and ward). Of the ₹91,00,000 budget, ₹82,64,048 (91%) is spent across 165 jobs, with Konkan Roadcon Pvt Ltd (synthetic) the largest by spend. Billing scores 90 and durability 52, about as expected, yet ₹17,41,105 went on fixes that failed within 30 days. The records show ₹4,02,110 in question: 3 bills above 1.5 times the rate card, 2 duplicate bills, and 7 payments (₹3,03,578) made on roads still within the contractor's guarantee period. 29 issues remain open and overdue. With ₹8,35,952 left, fix first the open manhole on Andheri Kurla Road (₹47,629), where 3 accidents, 1 fatal, occurred and a school is near. Next, the open manhole on Western Express Highway (₹47,629), also near a school. Third, a pump for waterlogging on Mahakali Caves Road (₹64,251), the ambulance route to Trauma Care Centre.]]></description><ExtendedData><Data name="ward_code"><value>K/E</value></Data><Data name="ward_name"><value>Andheri East, Vile Parle East, Jogeshwari East</value></Data><Data name="zone"><value>Zone 3</value></Data><Data name="grade"><value>B</value></Data><Data name="score"><value>64</value></Data><Data name="budget_inr"><value>9100000</value></Data><Data name="spend_inr"><value>8264048</value></Data><Data name="money_in_question_inr"><value>402110</value></Data><Data name="open_overdue_issues"><value>29</value></Data></ExtendedData><Polygon><outerBoundaryIs><LinearRing><coordinates>72.88851,19.15088 72.85669,19.14006 72.84149,19.09448 72.86847,19.09046 72.88658,19.09888 72.8993,19.12281 72.88851,19.15088</coordinates></LinearRing></outerBoundaryIs></Polygon></Placemark><Placemark><name>Ward K/W · grade C</name><styleUrl>#grade-C</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Grade C</b> (50 of 100; 50 is as expected for these jobs)<br/>Spent ₹78,45,240 of ₹89,00,000 (88%) on 143 jobs<br/>On fixes that failed within 30 days: ₹18,66,600<br/>In question: ₹20,93,883 (10 over-billed, 3 duplicates, 29 paid under DLP)<br/>Open problems past their SLA: 25<br/><br/>K/W ward scores 50 (grade C), meaning about as expected for these jobs, given method, rain and ward. Of the ₹89,00,000 budget, ₹78,45,240 (88%) is spent across 143 jobs, leaving ₹10,54,760. Repairs held less well than hoped: ₹18,66,600 went on fixes that failed within 30 days, and durability scored 46. Billing scored 44, and ₹20,93,883 is in question. The records show 10 bills above 1.5 times the rate card, 3 duplicate bills, and 29 payments (₹17,14,069) on roads still under the contractor's guarantee period. 25 issues remain open and overdue. Next fixes are three open or broken manholes, a 24-hour safety issue. Juhu Tara Road (₹47,629) is near a flood-prone subway and had an accident. SV Road (₹47,629) had 4 accidents and is near a school. Link Road costs ₹0 if the original contractor is called under the guarantee, and it is also near the school.]]></description><ExtendedData><Data name="ward_code"><value>K/W</value></Data><Data name="ward_name"><value>Andheri West, Juhu, Vile Parle West</value></Data><Data name="zone"><value>Zone 4</value></Data><Data name="grade"><value>C</value></Data><Data name="score"><value>50</value></Data><Data name="budget_inr"><value>8900000</value></Data><Data name="spend_inr"><value>7845240</value></Data><Data name="money_in_question_inr"><value>2093883</value></Data><Data name="open_overdue_issues"><value>25</value></Data></ExtendedData><Polygon><outerBoundaryIs><LinearRing><coordinates>72.80218,19.15778 72.8,19.15 72.80527,19.09727 72.84102,19.09429 72.84149,19.09448 72.85669,19.14006 72.80218,19.15778</coordinates></LinearRing></outerBoundaryIs></Polygon></Placemark><Placemark><name>Ward P/S · grade C</name><styleUrl>#grade-C</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Grade C</b> (51 of 100; 50 is as expected for these jobs)<br/>Spent ₹43,49,997 of ₹48,00,000 (91%) on 82 jobs<br/>On fixes that failed within 30 days: ₹3,40,751<br/>In question: ₹7,92,887 (5 over-billed, 1 duplicates, 14 paid under DLP)<br/>Open problems past their SLA: 18<br/><br/>P/S (Goregaon) scored 51, gra