 of 100. Of the ₹77,00,000 budget, ₹70,06,462 (91%) is spent across 141 jobs, leaving ₹6,93,538. A score of 50 means &quot;as expected for these jobs, given method, rain and ward,&quot; so durability at 50 is average, but ₹18,16,577 still went on fixes that failed within 30 days. About ₹9,65,363 is in question: 7 bills were above 1.5 times the rate card, 2 were duplicate bills, and 20 payments (₹6,14,828) were made on roads still under the contractor's guarantee period. 24 issues are open and overdue. The next three fixes are the broken manhole on Malad Subway (₹47,629), because it is the most urgent and 2 road accidents happened there last year, then dewatering pumps on Marve Road and Malad Subway (₹64,251 each). Both sites sit close to the subway, which floods in heavy rain and at big tides.]]></description><ExtendedData><Data name="ward_code"><value>P/N</value></Data><Data name="ward_name"><value>Malad</value></Data><Data name="zone"><value>Zone 4</value></Data><Data name="grade"><value>C</value></Data><Data name="score"><value>59</value></Data><Data name="budget_inr"><value>7700000</value></Data><Data name="spend_inr"><value>7006462</value></Data><Data name="money_in_question_inr"><value>965363</value></Data><Data name="open_overdue_issues"><value>24</value></Data></ExtendedData><Polygon><outerBoundaryIs><LinearRing><coordinates>72.81659,19.20926 72.80594,19.17121 72.89007,19.18218 72.81659,19.20926</coordinates></LinearRing></outerBoundaryIs></Polygon></Placemark><Placemark><name>Ward R/S · grade C</name><styleUrl>#grade-C</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Grade C</b> (58 of 100; 50 is as expected for these jobs)<br/>Spent ₹66,42,234 of ₹66,00,000 (101%) on 121 jobs<br/>On fixes that failed within 30 days: ₹10,20,154<br/>In question: ₹8,82,095 (7 over-billed, 0 duplicates, 11 paid under DLP)<br/>Open problems past their SLA: 21<br/><br/>R/S (Kandivali) scores a C, 58 out of 100, where 50 means &quot;as expected for these jobs, given method, rain and ward&quot;. Of the ₹66,00,000 budget, ₹66,42,234 was spent on 121 jobs (101%), leaving it ₹42,234 over. The repairs held only partly. Durability scored 59, and ₹10,20,154 went on fixes that failed within 30 days. ₹8,82,095 is in question: 7 bills were above 1.5 times the rate card, and 11 payments (₹5,43,742) were made on roads still under the contractor's guarantee period. No duplicate bills were found, but 21 issues remain open and overdue. The next three fixes are:

