ospital.]]></description><ExtendedData><Data name="ward_code"><value>R/C</value></Data><Data name="ward_name"><value>Borivali</value></Data><Data name="zone"><value>Zone 7</value></Data><Data name="grade"><value>D</value></Data><Data name="score"><value>43</value></Data><Data name="budget_inr"><value>2900000</value></Data><Data name="spend_inr"><value>3312447</value></Data><Data name="money_in_question_inr"><value>1461912</value></Data><Data name="open_overdue_issues"><value>20</value></Data></ExtendedData><Polygon><outerBoundaryIs><LinearRing><coordinates>72.92148,19.22941 72.82726,19.24736 72.82087,19.22452 72.90952,19.20975 72.92148,19.22941</coordinates></LinearRing></outerBoundaryIs></Polygon></Placemark><Placemark><name>Ward R/N · grade C</name><styleUrl>#grade-C</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Grade C</b> (58 of 100; 50 is as expected for these jobs)<br/>Spent ₹35,33,838 of ₹48,00,000 (74%) on 82 jobs<br/>On fixes that failed within 30 days: ₹11,60,682<br/>In question: ₹5,78,060 (0 over-billed, 1 duplicates, 22 paid under DLP)<br/>Open problems past their SLA: 10<br/><br/>R/N (Dahisar) scores 58, grade C, where 50 means as expected for these jobs given method, rain and ward. Of the ₹48,00,000 budget, ₹35,33,838 (74%) has been spent across 82 jobs, leaving ₹12,66,162. Repairs held less well than the billing did: durability scores 45, and ₹11,60,682 went on fixes that failed within 30 days. Billing scores 66, and no bill was above 1.5 times the rate card. Still, ₹5,78,060 is in question, including one duplicate bill and 22 payments (₹5,35,961) made on roads still under the contractor's guarantee period. Ten issues are open and overdue. The next three fixes are all on Western Express Highway, and each can be done at no cost by calling the original contractor under that guarantee. The open manhole and the cave-in come first, as both are severity 5 with a 24-hour deadline. The pothole, near a school, comes third. All three sit 424 m from Dahisar Subway, which floods often, and an accident was recorded nearby in 2024-25.]]></description><ExtendedData><Data name="ward_code"><value>R/N</value></Data><Data name="ward_name"><value>Dahisar</value></Data><Data name="zone"><value>Zone 7</value></Data><Data name="grade"><value>C</value></Data><Data name="score"><value>58</value></Data><Data name="budget_inr"><value>4800000</value></Data><Data name="spend_inr"><value>3533838</value></Data><Data name="money_in_question_inr"><value>578060</value></Data><Data name="open_overdue_issues"><value>10</value></Data></ExtendedData><Polygon><outerBoundaryIs><LinearRing><coordinates>72.92998,19.2393 72.88,19.275 72.835,19.275 72.82726,19.24736 72.92148,19.22941 72.92998,19.2393</coordinates></LinearRing></outerBoundaryIs></Polygon></Placemark><Placemark><name>Ward L · grade C</name><styleUrl>#grade-C</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Grade C</b> (48 of 100; 50 is as expected for these jobs)<br/>Spent ₹1,30,43,418 of ₹1,19,00,000 (110%) on 232 jobs<br/>On fixes that failed within 30 days: ₹18,20,204<br/>In question: ₹44,35,438 (8 over-billed, 4 duplicates, 52 paid under DLP)<br/>Open problems past their SLA: 30<br/><br/>Ward L (Kurla) scores 48, grade C; 50 means as expected for these jobs, given method, rain and ward. Across 232 jobs, ₹1,30,43,418 was spent against a ₹1,19,00,000 budget (110%). Repairs mostly held (durability 64), but ₹18,20,204 went on fixes that failed within 30 days. Billing scores lowest, at 29. The records show 8 bills above 1.5 times the rate card, 4 duplicate bills, and 52 payments (₹39,59,357) made on roads still under the contractor's guarantee period (DLP). In all, ₹44,35,438 is in question, and 30 issues are overdue. Next, call the original contractor under the guarantee, at no cost, to fix the cave-in, the broken manhole and the waterlogging on Kurla Andheri Road. All three are urgent and lie near Kamani Junction, which floods often. Three road-condition accidents happened here in 2024-25.]]></description><Extende