rd_name"><value>Govandi, Mankhurd, Deonar</value></Data><Data name="zone"><value>Zone 5</value></Data><Data name="grade"><value>C</value></Data><Data name="score"><value>52</value></Data><Data name="budget_inr"><value>9100000</value></Data><Data name="spend_inr"><value>7235685</value></Data><Data name="money_in_question_inr"><value>1531499</value></Data><Data name="open_overdue_issues"><value>18</value></Data></ExtendedData><Polygon><outerBoundaryIs><LinearRing><coordinates>72.91926,19.00739 72.955,19.02 72.97447,19.09789 72.96809,19.09805 72.91253,19.07026 72.91926,19.00739</coordinates></LinearRing></outerBoundaryIs></Polygon></Placemark><Placemark><name>Ward M/W · grade C</name><styleUrl>#grade-C</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Grade C</b> (46 of 100; 50 is as expected for these jobs)<br/>Spent ₹46,89,823 of ₹44,00,000 (107%) on 87 jobs<br/>On fixes that failed within 30 days: ₹11,50,699<br/>In question: ₹14,51,533 (4 over-billed, 0 duplicates, 23 paid under DLP)<br/>Open problems past their SLA: 15<br/><br/>Chembur (M/W) scores 46 out of 100, grade C. A score of 50 means about what you would expect for these jobs given method, rain and ward, so this is slightly below. The ward has spent ₹46,89,823 on 87 jobs against a ₹44,00,000 budget (107%), which is ₹2,89,823 over. Repairs often did not hold: ₹11,50,699 went on fixes that failed within 30 days. About ₹14,51,533 is in question. Four bills were above 1.5 times the rate card, and 23 payments, totalling ₹12,75,227, were made on roads still within the contractor's guarantee period. No duplicate bills appear, but 15 issues are open and overdue. The next three fixes are all on RC Marg, near flood-prone Chembur Shell Colony. First is the broken manhole, the most urgent because it is a top-severity hazard and an accident was recorded there; the original contractor should fix it at no cost. Second is waterlogging near a school, needing a pump at ₹64,251. Third is waterlogging at the accident spot, with a pump at no cost under the guarantee.]]></description><ExtendedData><Data name="ward_code"><value>M/W</value></Data><Data name="ward_name"><value>Chembur</value></Data><Data name="zone"><value>Zone 5</value></Data><Data name="grade"><value>C</value></Data><Data name="score"><value>46</value></Data><Data name="budget_inr"><value>4400000</value></Data><Data name="spend_inr"><value>4689823</value></Data><Data name="money_in_question_inr"><value>1451533</value></Data><Data name="open_overdue_issues"><value>15</value></Data></ExtendedData><Polygon><outerBoundaryIs><LinearRing><coordinates>72.90508,19.00238 72.91926,19.00739 72.91253,19.07026 72.90362,19.07331 72.87598,19.04893 72.90508,19.00238</coordinates></LinearRing></outerBoundaryIs></Polygon></Placemark><Placemark><name>Ward N · grade C</name><styleUrl>#grade-C</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Grade C</b> (56 of 100; 50 is as expected for these jobs)<br/>Spent ₹59,99,557 of ₹62,00,000 (97%) on 112 jobs<br/>On fixes that failed within 30 days: ₹9,70,747<br/>In question: ₹10,43,853 (6 over-billed, 3 duplicates, 15 paid under DLP)<br/>Open problems past their SLA: 19<br/><br/>Ward N (Ghatkopar, Vikhroli) scores 56, grade C; a score of 50 means as expected for these jobs, given method, rain and ward. Of the ₹62,00,000 budget, ₹59,99,557 (97%) is spent across 112 jobs, leaving ₹2,00,443. Repairs mostly held (durability 60), but ₹9,70,747 went on fixes that failed within 30 days. Records put ₹10,43,853 in question: 6 bills above 1.5 times the rate card, 3 duplicate bills, and 15 payments (₹7,05,327) made on roads still within the contractor's guarantee period. Also, 19 issues are open and overdue. The next three fixes are all on LBS Marg, which lies 321 m from a dip that floods on heavy-rain days and at big tides, and is the ambulance road to Rajawadi Hospital. First, a dewatering pump for waterlogging (₹64,251). Second, desilting the choked drain (₹73,252). Third, a hot mix pothole patch (₹16,437). Clearing the water first should help the patch last.]]></description><ExtendedData><Data name="ward_code"><value>N</value></Data><Data name="ward_name"><value>Ghatkopar, Vikhroli</value></Data><Data name="zone"><value>Zone 6</value></Data><Data name="grade"><value>C</value></Data><Data name="score"><value>56</value></Data><Data name="budget_inr"><value>6200000</value></Data><Data name="spend_inr"><value>5999557</value></Data><Data name="money_in_question_inr"><value>1043853</value></Data><Data name="open_overdue_issues"><value>19</value></Data></ExtendedData><Polygon><outerBoundaryIs><LinearRing><coordinates>72.8993,19.12281 72.88658,19.09888 72.90362,19.07331 72.91253,19.07026 72.96809,19.09805 72.8993,19.12281</coordinates></LinearRing></outerBoundaryIs></Polygon></Placemark><Placemark><name>Ward S · grade C</name><styleUrl>#grade-C</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Grade C</b> (52 of 100; 50 is as expected for these jobs)<br/>Spent ₹74,89,270 of ₹95,00,000 (79%) on 123 jobs<br/>On fixes that failed within 30 days: ₹22,19,613<br/>In question: ₹13,78,355 (6 over-billed, 3 duplicates, 16 paid under DLP)<br/>Open problems past their SLA: 16<br/><br/>Ward S (Bhandup, Powai, Kanjurmarg) scores 52, grade C, where 50 means as expected for these jobs, given method, rain and ward. Of the ₹95,00,000 budget, ₹74,89,270 (79%) is spent across 123 jobs, leaving ₹20,10,730. Repairs held poorly: durability scores 34, and ₹22,19,613 went on fixes that failed within 30 days. ₹13,78,355 is in question: 6 bills above 1.5 times the rate card, 3 duplicate bills, and 16 payments, ₹9,59,710 in all, on roads still under the contractor's guarantee period. 16 issues are open and overdue. Next fixes: first, a dewatering pump on Powai Adi Shankaracharya Marg for waterlogging, as it is the ambulance road to Bhandup Maternity Home and near a flood-prone road. Second, a hot mix patch on the same road, where 7 complaints and 36 &quot;me too&quot; reports wait. Third, a pump on LBS Marg, since waterlogging has a 48-hour deadline and the road is near the same flood-prone stretch.]]></description><ExtendedData><Data name="ward_code"><value>S</value></Data><Data name="ward_name"><value>Bhandup, Powai, Kanjurmarg</value></Data><Data name="zone"><value>Zone 6</value></Data><Data name="grade"><value>C</value></Data><Data name="score"><value>52</value></Data><Data name="budget_inr"><value>9500000</value></Data><Data name="spend_inr"><value>7489270</value></Data><Data name="money_in_question_inr"><value>1378355</value></Data><Data name="open_overdue_issues"><value>16</value></Data></ExtendedData><Polygon><outerBoundaryIs><LinearRing><coordinates>72.97447,19.09789 72.98176,19.12706 72.90098,19.18512 72.89782,19.18145 72.88851,19.15088 72.8993,19.12281 72.96809,19.09805 72.97447,19.09789</coordinates></LinearRing></outerBoundaryIs></Polygon></Placemark><Placemark><name>Ward T · grade C</name><styleUrl>#grade-C</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Grade C</b> (46 of 100; 50 is as expected for these jobs)<br/>Spent ₹39,53,564 of ₹51,00,000 (78%) on 65 jobs<br/>On fixes that failed within 30 days: ₹16,77,820<br/>In question: ₹5,51,198 (6 over-billed, 0 duplicates, 12 paid under DLP)<br/>Open problems past their SLA: 17<br/><br/>Ward T (Mulund) scores 46 out of 100, grade C, where 50 means about what is expected for these jobs given method, rain and ward. Of the ₹51,00,000 budget, ₹39,53,564 (78%) is spent across 65 jobs, mostly with Arabian Sea Engineering (synthetic). Repairs did not hold well: ₹16,77,820 went on fixes that failed within 30 days. ₹5,51,198 is in question, including 6 bills above 1.5 times the rate card and 12 payments, ₹4,55,154 in all, made on roads still under the contractor's guarantee period. No duplicate bills appear. 17 issues remain open and overdue. With ₹11,46,436 left, fix next: Devidayal Road waterlogging, the ambulance route to the hospital; Eastern Express Highway waterlogging, which carries heavy bus and vehicle traffic; and Devidayal Road's broken manhole, near a school and a 24-hour deadline.]]></description><ExtendedData><Data name="ward_code"><value>T</value></Data><Data name="ward_name"><value>Mulund</value></Data><Data name="zone"><value>Zone 6</value></Data><Data name="grade"><value>C</value></Data><Data name="score"><value>46</value></Data><Data name="budget_inr"><value>5100000</value></Data><Data name="spend_inr"><value>3953564</value></Data><Data name="money_in_question_inr"><value>551198</value></Data><Data name="open_overdue_issues"><value>17</value></Data></ExtendedData><Polygon><outerBoundaryIs><LinearRing><coordinates>72.98176,19.12706 72.985,19.14 72.985,19.2 72.92998,19.2393 72.92148,19.22941 72.90952,19.20975 72.90098,19.18512 72.98176,19.12706</coordinates></LinearRing></outerBoundaryIs></Polygon></Placemark></Folder><Folder><name>Roads: red flagged, orange paid under DLP</name><Placemark><name>Shahid Bhagat Singh Marg (RD0001)</name><styleUrl>#road-plain</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Shahid Bhagat Singh Marg</b> (RD0001), ward A<br/>Arterial, Asphalt<br/>Nothing flagged]]></description><ExtendedData><Data name="road_id"><value>RD0001</value></Data><Data name="road_name"><value>Shahid Bhagat Singh Marg</value></Data><Data name="ward_code"><value>A</value></Data><Data name="road_type"><value>Arterial</value></Data><Data name="surface"><value>Asphalt</value></Data><Data name="flags"><value>0</value></Data><Data name="money_in_question_inr"><value>0</value></Data></ExtendedData><LineString><tessellate>1</tessellate><coordinates>72.82866,18.920691 72.828663,18.922664</coordinates></LineString></Placemark><Placemark><name>Shahid Bhagat Singh Marg (RD0002)</name><styleUrl>#road-dlp</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Shahid Bhagat Singh Marg</b> (RD0002), ward A<br/>Arterial, Concrete (CC)<br/>In question: ₹39,223 across 3 flags<ul><li>WO25-02019: Shahid Bhagat Singh Marg (RD0002) was resurfaced on 2024-05-04 and is under its Defect Liability Period, yet BMC paid ₹19,888; the original contractor should have repaire